
* To ignore some file while commiting.
* Create one hidden file ".gitignore" and enter file format which you want to ignore.

Ex:-    vi .gitignore
enter-  *.css
        *.java   ---------> (*) means ignore .java file


- git add .gitignore
- git commit -m "latest update ignore .java"
- git status

# Create some file= Ex:- touch file1.txt file2.txt file3.java file4.css

- ls
- git status
- git commit -m "my text files only"


-----------------------------------------------
# Ipmortant to remember-

- git log -1       (It display the latest commit updates)
- git log -2       (It dispaly the last 2 updates)
- git log --oneline         (It will display all updates in oneline)
- git log --grep "ignore"   (it will display a specific word in git log) (Find the commit-id in specific word)


